capability subscribe-estate-live-observation
intent: Subscribe to the estate's live observation channel from any machine, as the legacy observer's GET /events allowed any signed-in session. The session store confirms the caller session. The selectors are the observer's: since (or Last-Event-ID) replays the retained channel after that sequence; run=current, last or <n> replays that run and keeps to it, and run=next keeps to the next run, each chosen by select-estate-live-observation; without since or run only new publications arrive; a run or since the observer refused is refused as it did, 400 invalid_run or invalid_since. The answer is the stream-estate directive the hosting facade follows: the opening frame retry: 3000, the replay, : replay-complete, each new frame, : keep-alive while quiet, and : session-ended when the session expires or a recheck through check-api-session, at the given interval, cannot confirm it; the x-observer-instance header names the channel.
outcome: a host directive (application/vnd.sfx.host-directive+json) stream-estate; a 400 invalid_run or invalid_since; or EVIDENCE_SESSION_REQUIRED
inquiry: May this caller watch the estate live, and from where?
input contract subscribe-estate-live-observation-request.v1 {"type":"object","properties":{"principalId":{"type":"string"},"sessionId":{"type":"string"},"since":{"type":"string"},"run":{"type":"string"},"graphId":{"type":"string"},"recheckMilliseconds":{"type":"integer"}}}
output contract subscribe-estate-live-observation-result.v1 {"type":"object"}
cli display outcome as json
scenario subscribe-estate-live-observation root terminal
given: the caller principal and session, and the observer's optional since, run and graphId
when: the session store reads the caller session and the selectors are read
then: the outcome is the stream directive, the selector refusal, or EVIDENCE_SESSION_REQUIRED
operation subscribe-estate-live-observation.read-prepare kind invoke-port port subscribe-estate-live-observation-read-prepare
operation subscribe-estate-live-observation.read kind invoke-port port subscribe-estate-live-observation-read
operation subscribe-estate-live-observation.answer kind invoke-port port subscribe-estate-live-observation-answer
platform bind subscribe-estate-live-observation-read-prepare
platform: sda-authority-transformation-port.v1
config: {"expression":{"op":"object","fields":{"executionTarget":{"op":"literal","value":"sql-database-reader"},"executionNamespace":{"op":"literal","value":"sidefx:capabilities"},"executionScenario":{"op":"literal","value":"sql-database-reader"},"inputType":{"op":"literal","value":"json"},"dispatchRequest":{"op":"object","fields":{"dataSource":{"op":"literal","value":"sfx-identity-database"},"statement":{"op":"literal","value":"SET NOCOUNT ON; DECLARE @principal_id uniqueidentifier = TRY_CONVERT(uniqueidentifier, JSON_VALUE(@input, '$.principalId')); DECLARE @session_id uniqueidentifier = TRY_CONVERT(uniqueidentifier, JSON_VALUE(@input, '$.sessionId')); DECLARE @expires datetimeoffset(7) = (SELECT s.expires_at FROM [identity].session s JOIN [identity].principal p ON p.principal_id = s.principal_id WHERE s.session_id = @session_id AND s.principal_id = @principal_id AND s.revoked_at IS NULL AND s.expires_at > SYSUTCDATETIME() AND p.active = 1); SELECT (SELECT JSON_VALUE(@input, '$.since') AS since, JSON_VALUE(@input, '$.run') AS run, JSON_VALUE(@input, '$.graphId') AS graphId, LOWER(CONVERT(varchar(36), @principal_id)) AS principalId, LOWER(CONVERT(varchar(36), @session_id)) AS sessionId, @expires AS sessionExpiresAt, CONVERT(bit, CASE WHEN @expires IS NULL THEN 0 ELSE 1 END) AS sessionLive, COALESCE(TRY_CONVERT(int, JSON_VALUE(@input, '$.recheckMilliseconds')), 5000) AS recheckMilliseconds FOR JSON PATH, WITHOUT_ARRAY_WRAPPER, INCLUDE_NULL_VALUES) AS value;"},"resultColumn":{"op":"literal","value":"value"},"input":{"op":"path","path":""}}}}}}
platform bind subscribe-estate-live-observation-read
